(GRM-16: loop_expansion ::= "each" name "from" expr ("treating" expr "as"
 expr)? - the shared expansion clause used by print_stmt (GRM-15), args
 (GRM-09), append_stmt's second form, and for_stmt's "in" form. Its
 "treating" substitution is confirmed working when the expansion sits
 under Print (GRM-15) or bare `each x from list` (below). It is a
 confirmed NO-OP under append_stmt specifically - see Discrepancy 3 -
 which is that production's own bug, not this one's; this row is clean.
 Cross-ref BAS2 (basics-expansion.md), which maps this production's full
 claim set including grid/nested expansion.
